WEBVTT

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.940
Dear Lady Eliaria Jamil.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.610
How are you?

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:16.910
I departed Gimul and am on my way
to Lenaf on my own.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.580
I'm going to open up the second
Bamboo Forest shop there!

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.870
Wow, a second shop already?!

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:29.040
That's impressive, Mr. Ryoma!

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:42.220
I wonder what kind of people
I'll meet in the new town.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:46.230
Elia, I can't wait!

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:28.000
"Episode 3"
"Ryoma and the Poster Girl"

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.220
So this is Lenaf...

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:50.230
It's not as big as Gimul,
but it's so full of activity.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.020
Right, then.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.030
Mr. Pioro Saionji...

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:03.870
Master Glissela told me to get help
from this person while in Lenaf.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.160
Let's go find him!

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:17.210
So this is Mr. Pioro's shop.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:21.300
Saionji Trading Company... It's huge.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.800
Welcome.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:32.140
They seem really busy. I probably
shouldn't bother them right now.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.360
Should I come back later?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.270
Well, hmm...

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.480
Welcome.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.530
Huh?

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.660
Are you looking for something?

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.780
Oh, sorry. I'm not here for shopping.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.160
I need to meet with Mr. Pioro Saionji.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.500
Oh, you here to see my dad?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.750
Dad?

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.630
Excuse me. Are you here to meet my father?

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.130
Y-Yes.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.170
What's up?

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.510
Hey, Dad.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.970
This is Mr. Pioro?

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.930
What's this, Miyabi? Is he hitting on you?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.100
No way! What are you talking about?!

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.140
He isn't? Too bad.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:16.730
Why is that a bad thing?!

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.980
Anyway, this boy wants to talk to you.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.110
To me?

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:28.450
Nice to meet you. I'm Ryoma Takebayashi
from the town of Gimul.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:31.450
I was sent here by Master Glissela.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:36.920
Oh, so you're Ryoma!
Nice to meet you. I'm Pioro!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:40.340
Glissela told me about you,

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:45.880
that there's a kid who does an interesting
business--a laundry service using slimes.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.350
You want to start a branch here, right?

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:54.520
In that case, you have to go to the guild
to do a lot of paperwork.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:58.730
But don't worry, I've got you covered
from head to toe.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.320
Thank you.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.190
Huh?

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.320
What's wrong, Miyabi?

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:08.370
I mean, a branch of a business?

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.990
This kid? For real?

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.870
He doesn't seem that much older than me.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:19.630
In fact, he's only 11,
so he's one year younger than you.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.630
Eleven?!

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.880
Don't be so surprised,
you're making Ryoma uncomfortable.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:28.800
Oh, my apologies!

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:35.020
My name is Miyabi Saionji. My father and I
are honored to make your acquaintance.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:38.900
Thank you, it's a pleasure
to meet you as well.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:44.110
By the way, "Miyabi" was the name of
the daughter of the founder of our business.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.860
I thought it'd bring
a share of the good luck.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.280
Um, right.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.820
Where'd that come from?!

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:55.450
Um, did that person
achieve something great?

00:05:55.450 --> 00:06:01.840
Nope, she was a regular poster girl,
and had a regular and happy life.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:06.260
I see, so you want your daughter
to be happy like her...

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:12.140
No, I thought naming my daughter after the
founder's daughter would bring me good luck.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.180
You want the good luck for yourself?!

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.100
S-Sorry, I couldn't help it...

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:20.810
No, that was a good jab. Right, Miyabi?

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:26.150
Indeed. Wait, no! You have business
at the guild, right?

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.200
Go take him there already!

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.860
Right!

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:37.790
And so we're off, but there's not actually
a lot to do at the guild.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:38.910
Huh?

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:42.670
Glissela asked me to
take care of everything,

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:46.340
so I've already talked to them about
the real estate, the various paperwork,

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:49.760
and all the other bothersome stuff.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:55.930
All that's left is for you to look through
some documents and sign them.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:07:00.560
You took care of that much already...?

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:05.650
If I hadn't, Glissela would
bite my head off.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:09.900
Here we are. Let's get this over with.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.030
Right!

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:15.990
Huh? That building is
the Merchant's Guild?

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.760
The interior is impressive, too.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:38.390
You like what you see, Ryoma?
It used to be a fortress.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:39.850
A fortress?

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:43.440
The Merchant's Guild uses a fortress?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.570
No, not just the Merchant's Guild.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:51.900
The Adventurer's Guild, Craftsman's Guild,
and the Dragoon's Guild.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.280
There are four guilds in this place.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.410
The Dragoon's Guild?

00:07:57.410 --> 00:08:02.410
Oh, right. You wouldn't know.
Take a look outside.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:06.210
Wow...

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:12.340
That's impressive, I've never seen
so many large monsters.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:16.470
All of those monsters
work for the Dragoon's Guild.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:20.470
They've been gathered
to carry people and goods.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.480
All of them?!

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:29.530
By using flying monsters,
they can carry many goods quickly.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:34.660
But doing so requires a lot of facilities
to tend to the monsters.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:38.620
They use the fortress for that.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:43.500
I see. But then,
what about the other guilds?

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.630
That's what makes Lenaf special.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:49.170
The Adventurer's Guild
gathers raw material,

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:52.090
the Craftsman's Guild
turns them into goods.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:58.140
The Merchant's Guild sells those goods,
and the Dragoon's Guild transports them.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:02.100
That's how this town got bigger.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.060
I see...

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:10.570
And to top it off, the person who
came up with that whole setup

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.740
is my ancestor!

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:16.950
He even came up with
the cool name, "Airport."

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.370
Pretty good, don't you think?

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:21.290
R-Right...

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.250
Yes!

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:27.790
Airport? That's a direct word from Earth.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:33.050
When I heard the name "Saionji,"
I thought about the possibility,

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:37.550
but now I know for sure,
Mr. Pioro's ancestor was a transfer as well.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:41.680
So this is another way
a transfer can leave their mark.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:42.970
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.890
Oh, here he is. Ryoma.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.310
Coming!

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:55.440
Thank you so much for
setting all this up for me, Mr. Pioro.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:58.070
I should have no trouble
working on opening my shop now.

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:00.950
That was no big deal,
don't worry about it.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:05.040
After all, you're a bright newcomer
that Glissela has high hopes for.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.630
In other words, it's in my best interest
to get gratitude from you.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.840
Return the favor somehow
in the future, all right?

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.670
Yes, certainly.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:18.510
Nice response. I'm looking forward to it.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.220
Let's go take a look at the shop now.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.430
Yes.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.100
So this is the place...

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:29.770
Looks good, huh? Also...

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:31.940
It's across the street from my place.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:34.730
If you need anything,
don't hesitate to ask.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:41.410
Wow, thank you so much
for all of your support.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:45.660
Like I said, don't worry about it.
I'm a businessman.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:50.500
I just make sure I don't miss any opportunity,
including hunting for gratitude.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:56.510
Enough about me,
and enough standing around.

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:59.380
Let's go inside!

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.640
Whoa, Mr. Pioro!

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:04.760
The first floor is the shop area.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:07.850
The second floor has
meeting rooms and such.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:11.600
The previous owner's house
is on the premises, as well,

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:15.610
so you can use that as
the employees' dormitory, I guess.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:22.070
Yes. I think this place will be ready
as soon as I build the furniture.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:26.040
I'll contact Gimul immediately
and get them to send people.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.410
Drei!

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.830
Oh, it's a limour bird!

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.710
Yes, I tamed them recently.

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:39.670
Glissela told me you're a tamer,

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:43.970
but I didn't know you were so good at that,
on top of being a good businessman.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.640
I'm counting on you, Drei!

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:53.980
All right, now we just wait
for people to arrive.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.650
By the way, did you already
book an inn for the night?

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:57.690
Oh!

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:02.740
Looks like you forgot. Good, then.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:05.410
You should stay at our place
while you're here.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:06.530
Are you sure?

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:10.200
Of course. And look forward
to dinner, too.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.080
Dinner?

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:15.960
You haven't eaten anything decent
after you left Gimul, have you?

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:23.760
I didn't realize
travel food was so gross...

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:33.390
Food for newbie adventurers is supposed to
be cheap and durable, not taste good.

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:35.150
Don't worry, though!

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:39.730
Tonight, you'll eat something
so delicious and rare,

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:42.240
you'll forget about all of that!

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.450
Delicious and rare?

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:50.580
Not that I'd know. No way.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:56.080
Yeah, I do realize
I should work hard, too. Really.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:03.090
Miso soup, cooked fish, and rice?!

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:09.850
Ryoma, you know about these?
I wanted to surprise you.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.350
I'm totally surprised!

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:15.480
Mr. Pioro, can you get miso around here?!

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:21.480
Yep. Not just miso,
but mirin, vinegar, and soy sauce, too.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.440
Soy sauce, too?!

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.900
Mr. Ryoma, please calm down.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.570
Oh... S-Sorry.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:31.330
If you're that interested,
I'll pack you some later.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.790
Are you sure?!

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:38.130
Enough chit-chat.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:41.300
Eat your food before it gets cold.

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:43.420
Talk later.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:45.880
All right, Mr. Ryoma?

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.180
Yes!

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:08.410
Delicious!

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:13.410
So many memories...

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:20.290
Memories? Did you live in
a Dragonewt village or something?

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:27.090
Oh, no, my grandmother used to make these.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:32.390
Don't be so uptight, what's important
is that you like this food.

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:35.220
Besides, I'm a bit relieved.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.560
Huh?

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:40.560
You have a cute side, too,
that's more befitting of your age.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:45.690
I was impressed by how you had a business
and a second branch at age 11.

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:49.990
Thank you, but I was just lucky.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:54.490
I was fortunate enough to meet
some great people and get their help.

00:14:54.490 --> 00:15:00.040
If you can honestly say that at your age,
that's already quite impressive.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.170
Compared to that, Miyabi here...

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:05.050
You got a problem with me, Dad?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:10.510
See? I wish you spoke
more politely, like Ryoma.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:18.140
Can you really make it in the academy
at the royal capital? I'm worried.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:21.690
Miss Miyabi, are you going to the academy?

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:26.650
Yeah, to make connections
as a future businessperson.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:30.200
It sounds like a lot of rigid human
relations type stuff would come up,

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:33.320
so I really don't want to go...

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.700
You're that opposed?

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.800
By the way, what are your plans
from tomorrow, Ryoma?

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.010
It'll take some time for my staff
to arrive from Gimul,

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:54.930
so I'll prepare the shop and also
find some work as an adventurer.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:58.430
What? Mr. Ryoma,
you're an adventurer, too?

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:02.020
Yes, but I'm only a rank E.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.400
Rank E...

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:09.400
At your age, E is quite high, but...

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.070
Is something wrong?

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:16.330
Mr. Ryoma, there aren't many
E-ranked jobs in town right now.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.410
Huh?

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:21.040
There's a strong monster
prowling the outskirts of town.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:27.000
It's preventing people from
assigning quick jobs outside of town.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:33.340
The monster's even showing its face
on the highways. It's affecting business.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.930
What kind of monster is it?

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:39.140
A Smash boar, rank D.

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:41.770
Smash boar...

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:46.060
Where did I hear that name before?

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:48.770
Right! It was before I reincarnated.

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:51.650
Gain and the other gods told me about it.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:58.160
There are several people whose names I've
borrowed to establish an identity in this world.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:01.660
They wanted me to find
and use their heirlooms

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:06.790
that they've hidden in their hometown.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.670
That hometown,
the Great Forest of Schluss,

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:14.680
is one of the most dangerous places
in this world, home to many fierce monsters.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:18.430
The gods suggested that I fight some monsters
that are similar to those in the Great Forest

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:21.640
to prepare, before I went.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.980
--Smash boar... That was one of
the monsters they mentioned!

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.400
--Ryoma?
--Smash boar... That was one of
the monsters they mentioned!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:28.310
Mr. Ryoma?

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:31.440
What's wrong? You seemed lost in thought.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:38.450
Oh, um... The smash boar happens to be
a monster I always wanted to try and take down.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.950
Oh, what a great coincidence, then!

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:46.080
In that case, why don't you go out
and take care of it for us!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:50.710
Then if you brought it back to me,
its meat sells quite well...

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.250
Dad?

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:58.090
What are you talking about?
Mr. Ryoma is a rank E.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:00.680
What are you going to do
if he winds up hurt or something?

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:07.690
I know, I know, I'm just joking,
don't get so upset.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:10.900
There are some things
one should <i>never</i> joke about!

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.360
On top of that,
the "joke" wasn't even funny!

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.440
Dad, you're the worst.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:19.820
Ryoma, help me...

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:22.370
Umm...

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:28.000
Sorry, Ryoma,
I have to stay at work today.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.330
I'll have Miyabi accompany you today.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.380
I'm counting on you here, Miyabi.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.710
Gotcha!

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:36.260
Good, see ya.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:39.510
So, Mr. Ryoma, what'll it be today?

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.100
Let's see...

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:45.270
I'd like to go buy some lumber
to make furniture for the shop.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:48.850
Lumber, got it!

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:59.070
Oh, sounds like he's working hard.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:05.410
Ryoma! How's it going?
I found some spare time so I came by to--

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:06.830
Huh?!

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.840
What's going on?

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:19.590
Miyabi, what is this?

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:22.640
Don't ask me.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:25.970
Mr. Ryoma, what are these?

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:27.770
Slimes, of course.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.600
No, no, no!

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:31.850
What do you mean, "Slimes, of course"?!

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:35.110
Yeah! How are these slimes
able to use tools?!

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:36.940
I taught them, and they learned.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.490
What?!

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:45.030
Well, I'll wrap up work on this for today.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:47.830
I'll head off to
the Adventurer's Guild now.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.500
Um, right.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:50.910
Safe trip...

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:52.120
Yes!

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.000
Hey, Mr. Ryoma!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:20:00.380
Watch out for the Smash Boar!
Run away if you see it!

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:03.510
That said...

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:05.890
Now that I'm outside of town,

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:12.100
I can't help it if it attacks me, right?

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:16.320
Miss Miyabi was right.

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:20.360
There were so few rank E jobs.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:23.910
Hunting for herbs was
the best I could find.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:31.460
Right. No point in being down!

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:37.130
Okay, let's begin.
It's time to get to work, Slimes.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:42.680
Yes, this stash should be enough...

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:47.100
Or maybe too much.

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:54.560
Elia! She wrote back already!

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:59.320
Mr. Ryoma, thank you for your letter!

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:02.740
Congratulations on
starting your second shop!

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:07.910
I was so elated that I went and
told my family all about it!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:14.330
They were all so happy to hear
your business was going well!

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:19.710
It's quite impressive that you're
able to start a new shop already.

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:24.680
Please start many branches like this.

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:26.430
Then, perhaps...

00:21:29.810 --> 00:21:33.850
If possible, maybe one in
the royal capital, as well.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:40.150
I thought perhaps then,
I will be able to see you again sooner.

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:46.950
Mr. Ryoma, with your business growing,
I'm sure you'll have a lot more work to do.

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:52.700
Please don't overwork yourself
and take care of your health.

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:57.290
Yes, I'll be careful. Thank you, Elia.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:02.840
Smash boar!
